#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Alias Maker: a terminal window with a Database and your Custom Commands in its menu.

It runs your normal shell (fish on CachyOS), like Konsole. The ☰ menu adds:
  Database          every program on this PC, searchable, filled by a scan
                    the first time Alias Maker opens
  Custom Commands   appears once you've made your first command:
                    Custom Command List, Create, Edit, Delete
  Create Command    make your own phrase: doit <your phrase> runs the real command
  Terminal Settings the command log (on/off, and a table of what ran) and how to say yes

Deleting a custom command only deletes your alias, never the real command.

Usage: aliasmaker [--workdir DIR] [-e COMMAND...]
Needs: sudo pacman -S vte4 python-gobject
"""

